      "note": "THE SEAL VOCABULARY'S AXIS IS WHETHER THE SEAL WAS ASKED FOR, which is why three of its four words are measurements and only `open` is the absence of one — and why `sealed -> open` is the single transition that retires a measurement rather than recording a newer one. On 2026-09-08 a blanket re-seal made that transition 44 times and nothing refused it; it was caught by diffing one file by hand. Two acts close it, because a guard alone would have punished a caller who meant the right thing: persist_validation now refuses sealed|indeterminate|breached -> open unless the caller states `unsealing_because`, which then rides permanently inside the record's evidence (the escape is on the record, never ambient) and fires BEFORE the announce and the write, so a refused write leaves the standing record untouched; and `cairn test --seal` asks each proof what isolation its standing seal was taken at and reproduces THAT, so the ordinary re-seal never meets the guard at all. sealed->breached, sealed->indeterminate and open->sealed all pass unrefused: a guard blocking a newer RED would be Law 7 inverted at the door Law 7 exists for. THE PER-PROOF READ IS VISIBLE AS A DISTRIBUTION rather than a word: the tester's own eight re-sealed at netns=4 none=4, the twelve out-of-component proofs fingerprinting a file this voyage changed at netns=11 none=1, and every one of the nineteen carrying a seal at HEAD reproduced it with zero guard refusals — including the three the blanket sweep had reddened and build_inspector's test_inspector, which carries seal:open because it times out at 120s inside a netns. One typed flag would have had to be wrong for one of those groups. A SECOND DEFECT IN THE SAME FUNCTION was fixed here under ruling 2026-09-09-a-bug-the-voyage-uncovers-is-fixed-by-that-voyage: the --seal summary printed `total - n_red` persisted while its own next clause said 'a red seals its red' (49 proofs, 6 red, printed 43, 49 on disk) — a Law 7 lie misreporting the very count this ticket is about. Five teeth, green twice, both mutations bite. And two deviations from the chart are in the verdict rather than smoothed over: hypothesis 1's falsifier fixed a corpus SNAPSHOT where it meant an invariant, and the probe's `enough` holds a floor on the sealed COUNT where the spec named a RATIO — a ratio falls when someone honestly adds an unsealed proof, so it would poke the owner about the system working.",
